WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:06.142
I wanted to say here
that Penajóia isn't the neighbourhood

2
00:00:06.513 --> 00:00:09.044
you keep painting it as.

3
00:00:09.414 --> 00:00:15.806
Penajóia is a neighbourhood
made up of working people.

4
00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:21.455
Penajóia is made up
of Portuguese nationals,

5
00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:24.576
Portuguese-born,
Angolans and Cape Verdeans.

6
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:31.993
Penajóia isn't a neighbourhood
of criminals, of gangsters, as they say.

7
00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:35.460
These are people who left
their countries with the promise

8
00:00:35.544 --> 00:00:37.921
of work in Portugal,
and who arrived here...

9
00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:45.298
because of the housing crisis, they
had no options, and we found this gap.

10
00:00:45.768 --> 00:00:51.200
We found this gap here,
we built our houses, indeed.

11
00:00:51.795 --> 00:00:55.946
We live with dignity, we pay what we owe.

12
00:00:56.096 --> 00:00:57.770
As for electricity and water,

13
00:00:58.977 --> 00:01:02.927
electricity and water
don't simply depend on us.

14
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:10.149
When they say we don't want to pay for
water or electricity, that's not quite it.

15
00:01:10.859 --> 00:01:15.190
How are we going to pay for electricity
and water if the State denies us that?

16
00:01:17.121 --> 00:01:23.413
The IHRU says the City
Council is responsible,

17
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:30.090
because Penajóia
is in the municipality of Almada,

18
00:01:30.225 --> 00:01:33.049
and Almada City Council has
to take responsibility.

19
00:01:34.647 --> 00:01:41.159
The Council says it's the IHRU,
because the land belongs to the IHRU.

20
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:49.006
We're stuck in this back-and-forth.
Now they ask: how will we pay for water?

21
00:01:50.339 --> 00:01:51.986
We're working people.

22
00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:57.190
We pay taxes, contributions...
Good afternoon! We pay...

23
00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:02.668
But unfortunately,

24
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:08.940
the neighbourhood is how it is.

25
00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:13.670
A neighbour? Exactly.

26
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.807
My neighbour. All working people.

27
00:02:15.891 --> 00:02:23.891
Honest people, looking for a home
to live in, who have families, right?

28
00:02:26.155 --> 00:02:33.228
And I'm asking you, everyone: come
and get to know Penajóia from the inside.

29
00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:37.110
Come and find out what Penajóia really is.

30
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.791
So you don't judge us,

31
00:02:40.161 --> 00:02:47.755
don't paint us, don't paint
us as outcasts, as idle people,

32
00:02:48.045 --> 00:02:53.977
people with nothing to do,
who left their countries to come here.

33
00:02:54.888 --> 00:03:00.380
That's not quite it. The problem
is that there's a housing crisis.

34
00:03:00.845 --> 00:03:03.036
When we went to apply for visas,

35
00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:10.560
when people applied for work visas,
student visas, scholarship visas,

36
00:03:11.451 --> 00:03:17.204
the embassy never said there
was a housing crisis in Portugal.

37
00:03:17.398 --> 00:03:20.986
And also many of you,
who sometimes sit there judging us...

38
00:03:21.516 --> 00:03:29.516
Portugal has a housing crisis.
There are no houses. There are no homes.

39
00:03:30.561 --> 00:03:32.130
And we've already done this.

40
00:03:33.963 --> 00:03:41.963
We live here with dignity,
we live on our own income.

41
00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:47.163
We also pay our contributions
to the Portuguese State.

42
00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:50.065
We've contributed a lot to this country.

43
00:03:50.315 --> 00:03:56.950
The people here are all working people,
and we found a solution.

44
00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.138
We just want the IHRU and the Council
to decide; it's both their problem.

45
00:04:02.222 --> 00:04:02.978
They must decide.

46
00:04:03.062 --> 00:04:10.315
The IHRU is the body responsible
for having homes, housing for everyone.

47
00:04:10.465 --> 00:04:15.757
And the IHRU doesn't have housing
for the people who are here.

48
00:04:16.287 --> 00:04:20.718
It doesn't. And we didn't go
and squat in flats, as many do.

49
00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:25.420
We didn't go stealing, robbing places, no.

50
00:04:25.986 --> 00:04:29.466
We saw an opportunity,
a space, we built our houses,

51
00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:35.244
and I don't see anything wrong with that.
They've judged us so much. I don't see it.
